{"event_type":"review","id":"f046ddfb64f354b2d9758462fadfcba9db7b319ef44e66de34ab2255be623ddb","occurred_at":"2026-11-11T23:36:28Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4ec9e0ee314bf512b0693be730664a515385165ed3f7c02ed1132d18ab4507a8","sha256":"4ec9e0ee314bf512b0693be730664a515385165ed3f7c02ed1132d18ab4507a8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/40bb601d360dece79900be609bc567097bcea425167a76197cde3ee0c88168bb","sha256":"40bb601d360dece79900be609bc567097bcea425167a76197cde3ee0c88168bb"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9bb93deaff27e8c4ebd62466e84be4ffb479264c53db28329c66d2ea4b6dfdc9","sha256":"9bb93deaff27e8c4ebd62466e84be4ffb479264c53db28329c66d2ea4b6dfdc9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/628d1767c73db385dddf47efab78e8279b597b53a871cd4415efb30a0c14dc04","sha256":"628d1767c73db385dddf47efab78e8279b597b53a871cd4415efb30a0c14dc04"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0a44dbc5ce748e182de0fc93fd1e693528506cf84d81cffc58051658033ec538","sha256":"0a44dbc5ce748e182de0fc93fd1e693528506cf84d81cffc58051658033ec538"}],"attempt_id":"c592b05451bd311492ce7ea721e4ae6186d6434de5d599af7f22dd5da81f000d:0:1","base":"cfe295817e31ee521b733ccf9698eca2aefab289","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"883127ae7f04e4569117fe0dea49d997091e6f50","body":"**Remove the host-specific `OSError` case from the fixture set.**\n\n`emit.py:13-15` and `README.md:28-29` state that the generated bytes are identical on every Python 3.14 host. The `platform-time-error` case at `emit.py:1462` stores the message `[Errno 75] Value too large for defined data type` in `utilization.json:2274`. That text comes from the host C library, so a host with a different C library can produce a different message. The regenerated bytes then differ from the checked-in file, `--check` reports a stale fixture, and `--write` on that host replaces the expectation.\n\nRemove the case so the checked-in expectation contains no platform text, then regenerate the fixture:\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    cases.append(case(\"platform-time-error\", now=1e18))\n```\n\n</details>\n\nRun `python3 fixtures/a1-status/emit.py --write` to remove the entry from `utilization.json`. This drops coverage of the OS-error path. Keep the case only if the expectation records the error class without the message.","id":"6a0d79df24d13cecd2c341a8349f348aa71b3ae094e21486de400520eca9532f","intervals":[[1462,1462]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Remove the host-specific `OSError` case from the fixture set."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"883127ae7f04e4569117fe0dea49d997091e6f50","body":"**Recompute `equivalence` after applying overrides.**\n\n`_capture_document` computes `equivalence` before `capture.update(overrides)`. The bounded-preview loop at `apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py:761` passes `target=target`, so each receipt's stored `equivalence` identifies the default `TARGET`, not the target it records. Because `target` is an equivalence field, the stored value no longer matches the capture.\n\nThis can make the bounded items fail the binding check at `apps/crq-python/status_summary.py:98`, which raises `receipt binding mismatch` before the 32-target preview logic at `emit.py:752-753` is reached. The generated expectation would then cover the binding-mismatch path instead of the preview limit.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def _capture_document(paths: List[Dict[str, Any]], **overrides: Any) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n     capture = {\n         \"target\": TARGET,\n         \"tree\": TREE,\n         \"paths\": paths,\n         \"scope_digest\": review_receipt.digest(paths),\n         \"policy\": review_receipt.POLICY,\n         \"projection\": PROJECTION,\n         \"reviewer\": REVIEWER,\n         \"reviewer_version\": \"fixture\",\n     }\n-    capture[\"equivalence\"] = review_receipt.current_equivalence(capture)\n     capture.update(overrides)\n+    capture[\"equivalence\"] = review_receipt.current_equivalence(capture)\n     return capture\n```\n\n</details>","id":"9ceb5c7ea4323126140687fc04e598243b6f3505083a8a9abc10ad6b977c8a50","intervals":[[90,90]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Recompute `equivalence` after applying overrides."}],"head":"fcfb06f1033038638f7c8358e9c3a0f2a44adff8","head_tree":"fd9b086373c60203765fe780f899178a146a7825","input_scope":[{"blob":"39b8ca05b673a9a4b4e2bcd53d8f60c0f49689b0","intervals":[[1,80]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/README.md"},{"blob":"883127ae7f04e4569117fe0dea49d997091e6f50","intervals":[[1,2028]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/emit.py"},{"blob":"c7c9555635b3a5edd613bb5e64b0ff819babe52c","intervals":[[1,508]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/numeric-lineage.json"},{"blob":"b0b5401de0402da8239a464c7eec89b56a181e3c","intervals":[[1,280]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/numeric.json"},{"blob":"a48492b191b83e1402d98109816c508dc4a8ea55","intervals":[[1,608]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/passthrough-receipt.json"},{"blob":"9da7b37b686b5315e0f9bce9325b5e2099adec6a","intervals":[[1,1114]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/passthrough-summarize.json"},{"blob":"930d9398af18547fdb54353c5046509bde54e8bd","intervals":[[1,2278]],"path":"apps/crq-python/fixtures/a1-status/utilization.json"}],"job_id":"c592b05451bd311492ce7ea721e4ae6186d6434de5d599af7f22dd5da81f000d:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"39b8ca05b673a9a4b4e2bcd53d8f60c0f49689b0","disposition":"inc